o  theater um roscoe is a bit more uh  financial ambition  colin's just a normal guy  like he's gay and he uh you know he's  around  that scene but you know he he works at a  tailors  and he just he just wants to work  and be good at his job and have pride in  what he does  and then you know they they each have  their families who  find out at varying points  that their sons or  brothers or what have you are gay  and respond differently when we actually  meet roscoe for the first time  uh he has been  discovered already and his  family who's nigerian they are  praying about it they're planning to  send him away  he packs a bag comes down to the family  table in a dress tells them all to go  screw themselves and storms out  so that's our introduction to him richie  is  terrified to ever tell his family  because their behavior on a regular  basis  demonstrates very clearly that they will  not  be accepting uh at all  and he just hides that part of himself  from them colin is  i mean he's too shy to really be too  open with anybody it's actually one of  the most adorable things that's in the  first episode  he's having a conversation with someone  who's just met at his job  who's actually played by neil patrick  harris  and this guy is  you know he's he's a little flamboyant  he's uh you know he's a little sort of  fop-ish um but he's  he he can tell and but he  he gives colin an out he says you know  do you  have a girlfriend boyfriend do you wish  you did and sort of continuing down that  that um road and giving colin the chance  to  say oh yeah girlfriend no i wish i had a  girlfriend like he gives him an out  he doesn't pin him against the wall but  he gives them the chance to say it  and when colin says  i wish i had a boyfriend the relief  on his face but of course even this  first episode  which is largely a celebration of these  characters  and of their joy in their lives  and their connections with other people  are filled with portent  because you know what t